; bal -V and -X with --unrealized foot to zero for a journal with a
; payee-rewrite directive, as they do for the same journal without one.
; The Brokerage posting of the 2024/01/01 purchase is dated 2024/01/15,
; after the dollar fell from EUR 0.90 to EUR 0.80.  rewrite_posts copies
; the purchase, whose payee the rule matches, once, whole, keeping its
; date, so both postings are valued at cost on that date, the purchase
; adds nothing to the report total, and the change in the value of the
; lot is the one unrealized row, minus the --gain total.  When
; rewrite_posts copied each posting into a transaction of its own, dated
; by the posting, these reports kept the revaluation between postings
; instead: the -X EUR report totalled EUR10.00, and the -V report booked
; no unrealized gain and totalled $200.  The journal is that of
; unrealized-footing-posting-date.test with the directive added, and the
; output is that journal's; unrealized-account-rewrite.test covers
; account-rewrite.

payee-rewrite Buy  Purchase

P 2024/01/01 $ 0.90 EUR
P 2024/01/10 $ 0.80 EUR

2024/01/01 Buy
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL @ $150  ; [2024/01/15]
    Assets:Checking

P 2024/03/05 AAPL $170

test bal -X EUR --unrealized
           EUR160.00  Assets
          EUR1360.00    Brokerage
         EUR-1200.00    Checking
          EUR-160.00  Equity:Unrealized Gains
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -V --unrealized
                $200  Assets
               $1700    Brokerage
              $-1500    Checking
               $-200  Equity:Unrealized Gains
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -G -X EUR
           EUR160.00  Assets:Brokerage
end test
